# Retire opcode 9: dst/alias flags, offset, target(buffer/data/global/null/raw), frame start, unused.
# Keep data and callable authority in separate surviving buffers.
1 0 0 0 0 0
2 1 0 0 0 4
2 1 4 0 4 4
1 1 8 2 0 0
1 2 16 3 0 0
# Reject caller-owned, global, nonbase, narrowed and wrong-frame requests atomically.
9 0 0 1 2 0
9 0 0 2 0 0
9 0 1 0 0 0
9 64 0 0 0 0
9 0 0 0 3 0
9 0 0 3 0 0
9 0 0 4 0 0
# End data target in its owning frame. Stored split-copy aliases become stale;
# callable tokens in live buffers retain their targets/signatures.
9 0 0 1 0 0
9 0 0 1 0 0
# Retire only buffer0; other buffers and global remain live.
9 129 0 0 2 0
6 0 0 0 0 0
6 1 0 1 0 0
# End buffer1 through an exact base; repeated termination is expired.
9 1 0 0 2 0
9 1 0 0 2 0
# Zero length copies/sets still avoid access even with retired capabilities.
2 0 0 1 0 0
3 1 0 0 0 0
7 0 0 0 0 0
